<code>assert index >= 0 && index < \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; index < i && i < \old(this.size()) - 1; (this.get(i) == null) == (\old(this.get(i + 1)) == null) && (this.get(i) != null) => this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i + 1)));</code>

However, since the condition `(this.get(i) == null) == (\old(this.get(i + 1)) == null)` and `(this.get(i) != null) => this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i + 1)))` can be simplified to just checking the equality directly, the more concise form would be:

<code>assert index >= 0 && index < \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; index < i && i < \old(this.size()) - 1; (this.get(i) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i + 1)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert index>=0 && index<\old(this.size()) => \forall int i; index<i && i<\old(this.size())-1; (this.get(i) == null) == (\old(this.get(i+1)) == null) && (this.get(i) != null) => this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1)));</code>

This assert statement captures the essence of the comment, ensuring that for every valid index, the elements are shifted correctly and null values are handled appropriately.
